  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A, B$ be two distinct points on the parabola $y^{2}=4 x$. If the axis of the parabola touches a circle of radius $r$ having $A B$ as diameter, the slope of the line $A B$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "9KkbI",
      "text": "$-\\frac{1}{r}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "xukwh",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{r}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Dyw7j",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{r}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9nCdz",
      "text": "None of the above",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Centre of circle $=\\left(\\frac{t_{1}^{2}+t_{2}^{2}}{2},\\left(t_{1}+t_{2}\\right)\\right)$\r\nsince, circle touch the $x$ -axis, so equation of tangent is $y=0$\r\n$\\because$ Radius = Perpendicular distance from centre to the tangent\r\n$\\Rightarrow$ Radius $=\\left|t_{1}+t_{2}\\right|=r$\r\nSlope of $A B=\\frac{2}{t_{1}+t_{2}}=\\frac{2}{\\pm r}$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2018_mat_a46.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
